NOT FINISHED. No beacon has closed this ceremony, so its delta is a product
of participant scalars only -- sound if one of them was honest, but with
nothing anchoring it to a value they could not all have known in advance.

Still unchecked, by anything, ever:
  * that any participant drew their scalar unpredictably and destroyed it;
  * that the beacon was named before this ceremony opened.
Both rest on what people published about themselves, not on these artifacts.

Before deploying, put this key through the acceptance gate -- which deploys a
pool carrying exactly these bytes and requires it to accept a real transfer:
  TOS_ROOT=<a checkout with a built func/fift> cargo run --release \
    --manifest-path tools/shielded-pool-circuit/crosscheck/Cargo.toml \
    --example ceremony-gate -- <ceremony>

Then, for the state hash and the address these bytes imply:
  cargo run --manifest-path tools/shielded-pool-genesis/Cargo.toml \
    --bin genesis -- . out/manifest.json --verifying-key <the file above>
